H("672.d.4.C",3,"Before writing code, a programmer writes down the problem's description, purpose and:","goals",["jokes","menus","passwords"],"Define the target first.")
H("672.d.4.C",4,"A program must calculate the area of a rectangle. The input and expected output are part of the:","problem's goals",["screen's color","keyboard layout","file size"],"Clarify inputs and outputs.")
H("672.d.4.D",3,"Writing a small program that prints a message demonstrates coding:","proficiency",["indifference","avoidance","delay"],"Practice builds proficiency.")
H("672.d.4.D",4,"A student writes a program that asks a user's name and greets them. This shows the ability to develop:","a solution in a programming language",["a hardware device","a database table","a printer driver"],"Code solves problems.")
H("672.d.4.E",3,"To store a whole number such as 42, the best data type is:","integer",["string","Boolean","character"],"Integers hold whole numbers.")
H("672.d.4.E",4,"To store the text 'Hello', the best data type is:","string",["integer","float","Boolean"],"Strings hold text.")
H("672.d.4.F",3,"A named storage location whose value can change while a program runs is a:","variable",["constant label only","comment line","syntax rule"],"Variables store data.")
H("672.d.4.F",4,"In a game, a variable called score starts at 0 and increases when you win. This shows how a variable:","changes during the program",["never changes","is deleted at start","is a cable"],"Values vary.")
H("672.d.4.G",3,"The operator for multiplication in most programming languages is:","*",["+","-","%"],"Asterisk multiplies.")
H("672.d.4.G",4,"If x is 10 and y is 3, what does x % y return in most languages?","1",["3","7","0"],"Modulo gives the remainder.")
H("672.d.4.H",3,"Instructions run one after another in a program, in the order written. This is:","sequence",["selection","iteration","recursion"],"Sequence is order.")
H("672.d.4.H",4,"If a program prints 'A' then 'B' then 'C', the output order shows:","sequence",["iteration","branching","randomness"],"Order matters.")
H("672.d.4.I",3,"A statement that runs different code depending on whether something is true is a:","conditional statement",["comment","variable","constant"],"Conditionals select paths.")
H("672.d.4.I",4,"Which code idea checks whether a score is greater than 100 before showing 'Winner'?","if score > 100",["loop 100","print 100","set 100"],"If statements test conditions.")
H("672.d.4.J",3,"A loop that repeats a block of code is called:","iteration",["sequence","declaration","comment"],"Iteration repeats.")
H("672.d.4.J",4,"To make a sprite move 10 steps five times, a programmer should use a:","repeat loop",["comment","print command","random number"],"Loops avoid copying code.")
H("672.d.4.K",3,"A program that picks a different number each run to simulate a dice roll uses:","random numbers",["constants","comments","fixed values"],"Random values add variety.")
H("672.d.4.K",4,"A game generates a random number from 1 to 6. Which result is NOT possible?","7",["1","3","6"],"The range is 1 through 6.")
H("672.d.4.L",3,"Running a program with known inputs to see if it behaves as expected is:","testing",["decorating","formatting","naming"],"Tests check outcomes.")
H("672.d.4.L",4,"When a program's output differs from the intended outcome, the programmer should:","investigate and fix the cause",["delete the program","ignore the error","change the goal secretly"],"Testing reveals bugs.")
H("672.d.5.A",3,"Downloading a song without paying for it breaks laws about:","copyright",["font style","screen size","file names"],"Copyright protects music.")
H("672.d.5.A",4,"To ethically use an online article in a report, you should:","cite the source",["claim it as your own","remove the author's name","change the facts"],"Cite to give credit.")
H("672.d.5.B",3,"Software that is free to use but still owned by its creator is called:","freeware",["open source","proprietary only","pirated"],"Free does not always mean shareable code.")
H("672.d.5.B",4,"Which option lets you view and modify the code?","open source",["trialware","commercial license","locked app"],"Open source shares code.")
H("672.d.5.C",3,"Being polite and respectful in online messages shows proper digital:","etiquette",["clutter","lag","bandwidth"],"Manners apply online.")
H("672.d.5.C",4,"A district document spelling out what students may and may not do on school networks is called an acceptable use policy, which guides how to:","use school technology responsibly",["buy games","avoid homework","delete logs"],"AUPs define rules.")
H("672.d.5.D",3,"A password that mixes upper-case letters, numbers and symbols is considered:","strong",["weak","short","common"],"Complexity protects accounts.")
H("672.d.5.D",4,"Keeping antivirus software updated helps protect against:","new malware",["power outages","slow typing","low volume"],"Updates add protection.")
H("672.d.5.E",3,"Social media, smartphones and streaming are computing advances that have changed:","how society communicates",["only weather","only prices","only seasons"],"Technology shapes society.")
H("672.d.5.E",4,"Which is an ethical concern linked to facial recognition technology?","privacy and surveillance",["battery color","keyboard shape","monitor size"],"New tech raises ethical questions.")
H("672.d.5.F",3,"Because anyone can post online, users should check whether information is:","reliable",["colorful","loud","long"],"Reliability matters.")
H("672.d.5.F",4,"A viral post with no author or source should be:","verified before it is believed",["shared at once","accepted as true","saved as fact"],"Verify before trusting.")
H("672.d.6.A",3,"Which component is often called the 'brain' of the computer?","central processing unit",["monitor","speaker","mouse"],"The CPU processes instructions.")
H("672.d.6.A",4,"Temporary working memory that the CPU uses is:","RAM",["ROM","hard disk","USB cable"],"RAM holds active data.")
H("672.d.6.B",3,"Creating folders, renaming files and moving them is called file:","management",["destruction","corruption","encryption"],"Management keeps files in order.")
H("672.d.6.B",4,"A tool that shows which programs are using memory is a system:","monitor",["theme","wallpaper","font"],"System tools help manage resources.")
H("672.d.6.C",3,"Windows, macOS and Linux are different:","operating systems",["web browsers","search engines","word processors"],"Each OS has features.")
H("672.d.6.C",4,"Which operating system is typically open source?","Linux",["Windows","macOS","iOS"],"Linux code is public.")
H("672.d.6.D",3,"The operating system manages hardware, while an application helps a user:","perform a specific task",["power the computer","cool the processor","connect a cable"],"Apps do tasks.")
H("672.d.6.D",4,"A photo editor is an application, while the program that schedules the CPU is the:","operating system",["web page","spreadsheet","monitor"],"The OS runs the machine.")
H("672.d.6.E",3,"A scanner is a device used for:","input",["output only","processing only","cooling"],"Scanners bring data in.")
H("672.d.6.E",4,"A solid-state drive is an example of:","secondary storage",["primary memory","an output device","a power supply"],"SSDs keep data when off.")
# ---- 673 Computer Science II ----
H("673.d.1.A",3,"An internship at a software firm is useful because it lets a student:","see job duties in practice",["avoid all coding","skip school","ignore teammates"],"Hands-on experience clarifies the work.")
H("673.d.1.A",4,"Which source best describes the daily tasks of a database administrator?","a professional job description",["a restaurant menu","a bus map","a sports score"],"Postings list duties.")
H("673.d.1.B",3,"A credential earned by passing an exam that proves a skill is a:","certification",["wallpaper","cursor","icon"],"Certifications show skill.")
H("673.d.1.B",4,"A computer science portfolio is best used to:","show examples of your finished projects",["store passwords","hide your work","list favorite games"],"Portfolios demonstrate ability.")
H("673.d.1.C",3,"Studying a library's documentation to learn how to call a function is technical:","reading",["swimming","cooking","painting"],"Technical reading explains tools.")
H("673.d.1.C",4,"A clear README that explains how to run your program demonstrates technical:","writing",["skating","juggling","sketching"],"Clear docs help users.")
H("673.d.1.D",3,"Explaining your code to a teammate in plain language shows effective:","verbal communication",["silence","guessing","delay"],"Clear explanations help teams.")
H("673.d.1.D",4,"Nodding and keeping eye contact while a teammate speaks is an example of:","non-verbal communication",["syntax","compiling","debugging"],"Body language shows attention.")
H("673.d.1.E",3,"Breaking a large problem into smaller parts is a form of:","problem solving",["avoidance","guesswork","delay"],"Decomposition helps.")
H("673.d.1.E",4,"A developer compares several designs and picks the best using evidence. This is:","critical thinking",["random choice","copying","ignoring the problem"],"Evidence-based decisions.")
H("673.d.1.F",3,"A team member who shares work, listens and supports others demonstrates:","teamwork",["rivalry","isolation","blame"],"Teams share load.")
H("673.d.1.F",4,"Guiding a group toward a goal and encouraging members is:","leadership",["avoidance","interference","favoritism"],"Leaders motivate.")
H("673.d.1.G",3,"A programmer who respects users' private data meets an ethical and legal:","responsibility",["shortcut","gamble","trick"],"Protect user data.")
H("673.d.1.G",4,"Which action shows legal and ethical responsibility in computing?","following software license terms",["pirating software","cracking passwords","sharing private files"],"Obey license terms.")
H("673.d.1.H",3,"Using a schedule to finish a software project by the deadline is good:","time management",["procrastination","guessing","delay"],"Schedules keep work on track.")
H("673.d.1.H",4,"A student plans two hours each day for coding practice. This is an example of:","planning",["avoidance","random action","luck"],"Plans create habits.")
H("673.d.1.I",3,"Comparing tuition, courses and research options of colleges is comparing:","computer science programs",["lunch menus","dorm colors","parking spots"],"Compare to choose.")
H("673.d.1.I",4,"A student who wants to study robotics should check whether a program offers:","robotics courses and labs",["a large gym","a famous mascot","a long summer"],"Program fit matters.")
H("673.d.2.A",3,"Joining a coding club or online forum to share ideas and learn is participating in a:","learning community",["lonely contest","power grid","print shop"],"Communities help learners.")
H("673.d.2.A",4,"In a learning community, a student who answers others' questions is acting as a:","contributor",["bystander only","critic only","spectator only"],"Contributors give help.")
H("673.d.2.B",3,"Asking a mentor to review your code and improve it is:","seeking advice",["avoiding help","hiding mistakes","skipping review"],"Advice strengthens work.")
H("673.d.2.B",4,"A peer suggests simplifying a function. A good response is to:","consider the idea and test it",["reject it immediately","argue loudly","delete the program"],"Evaluate suggestions fairly.")
H("673.d.3.A",3,"Showing a clear label before a result, such as 'Total:', is properly labeling:","output",["input","memory","cables"],"Labels explain results.")
H("673.d.3.A",4,"Which output line is best labeled?","Total cost: 12.50",["12.50","???","@@@"],"A label explains the value.")
H("673.d.3.B",3,"A program that asks 'Enter your age:' before reading a value is creating an interactive:","input interface",["output cable","storage drive","power switch"],"Prompts guide users.")
H("673.d.3.B",4,"A helpful prompt tells the user what to:","enter",["delete","ignore","print"],"Prompts guide input.")
H("673.d.3.C",3,"Using meaningful variable names and indenting code improves:","readability",["file size","power use","bandwidth"],"Good style helps readers.")
H("673.d.3.C",4,"Which variable name best stores how well one learner did on an assessment?","studentGrade",["x1","zz","a"],"Descriptive names clarify purpose.")
H("673.d.3.D",3,"Showing a decimal value rounded to two places is formatting a:","data display",["power cord","password","network"],"Formatting shapes output.")
H("673.d.3.D",4,"A price of 5.5 should be displayed as 5.50 by using:","standard formatting",["random rounding","string reversing","deleting digits"],"Format for readability.")
H("673.d.3.E",3,"Drawing a line, circle or rectangle on the screen is creating simple:","vector graphics",["network cables","password hashes","email headers"],"Vector shapes are drawn from math.")
H("673.d.3.E",4,"Vector graphics can be scaled without losing quality because they are defined by:","mathematical descriptions",["pixels only","audio tracks","sound waves"],"Math scales cleanly.")
H("673.d.4.A",3,"A planning diagram that shows the steps of a solution using boxes and arrows is a:","flowchart",["spreadsheet","firewall","bookmark"],"Flowcharts plan logic.")
H("673.d.4.A",4,"Writing the logic of a program in plain-language steps before coding is called:","pseudocode",["machine code","binary","debugging"],"Pseudocode plans the algorithm.")
H("673.d.4.B",3,"A visual tool for planning a program at a high level is a:","flowchart or storyboard",["monitor","printer","router"],"Visual plans help.")
H("673.d.4.B",4,"A high-level program plan shows the overall steps without:","every detail of the code",["a goal","any ordering","an outcome"],"High-level means broad.")
H("673.d.4.C",3,"Breaking a goal into smaller jobs to solve it means identifying:","tasks and subtasks",["fonts and colors","files and folders","prizes and games"],"Decomposition.")
H("673.d.4.C",4,"For a program that grades a quiz, one subtask could be:","adding up the correct answers",["choosing a wallpaper","printing a poster","buying a laptop"],"Subtasks are smaller steps.")
H("673.d.4.D",3,"To store a person's name and age, a program needs suitable:","data types",["monitors","speakers","routers"],"Choose types for the data.")
H("673.d.4.D",4,"Which pair of data types best matches name and age?","string and integer",["Boolean and string","float and Boolean","array and image"],"Names are text; ages are numbers.")
H("673.d.4.E",3,"Using a function already written in another program instead of rewriting it is reusing:","existing code components",["new hardware","blank files","power cords"],"Reuse saves time.")
H("673.d.4.E",4,"A reusable component such as a function that calculates tax can be:","called by many parts of a program",["used only once","deleted after use","kept secret"],"Reusability is efficient.")
H("673.d.4.F",3,"After defining a problem and listing tasks, the next step is to:","design a solution",["quit the project","buy a game","delete notes"],"Design follows analysis.")
H("673.d.4.F",4,"A design might include a flowchart and a list of:","variables and functions needed",["favorite songs","vacation plans","lunch orders"],"A design describes the pieces.")
H("673.d.4.G",3,"Turning a flowchart into working instructions in a language is:","coding the solution",["drawing a map","printing a flyer","naming a file"],"Implementation follows design.")
H("673.d.4.G",4,"When coding from a design, you should follow the planned:","structure and logic",["random order","blank spaces only","comments only"],"Stay faithful to the plan.")
H("673.d.4.H",3,"A mistake such as a missing parenthesis is a:","syntax error",["logic error","run-time error","lexical decoration"],"Syntax errors break grammar rules.")
H("673.d.4.H",4,"A program that runs but gives wrong totals has a:","logic error",["syntax error","hardware error","lexical error only"],"Logic errors give wrong results.")
H("673.d.4.I",3,"Testing a program with both valid and invalid data helps check if it handles:","unexpected input",["only perfect input","nothing","only colors"],"Invalid data tests resilience.")
H("673.d.4.I",4,"If a program asks for an age and a user types 'abc', that input is:","invalid test data",["valid test data","the correct answer","an operator"],"Invalid data shows weaknesses.")
H("673.d.4.J",3,"Reading an error message to find the line of a problem is part of:","debugging",["decorating","copying","saving"],"Messages point to bugs.")
H("673.d.4.J",4,"Which resource helps solve a bug in a library function?","language documentation",["a random poster","a menu","a flyer"],"Docs explain correct use.")
